From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:49:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] power: supply: iceland-supervooc: assert the 7.3 A
 ceiling at build time

The parameter checks already refuse an ask above 73 (7.3 A, stock's highest).
Add a static_assert over the tables that feed the ask (V3B_CAP_MAX,
V3_STOCK_ASK, V4_ENV_A0), so a later edit cannot raise it unnoticed.

Based on dappermint/iceland-supervooc commit 614469fabe59 ("ci: run the host tests on every push");
builds on DocZ13's SC8547D handover in iceland-linux issue #2 and on OnePlus's open-source oplus_chg code.

Link: https://github.com/dappermint/iceland-supervooc

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c b/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c
index 3cb3c01a02125..dc893b7dbea8b 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/iceland-supervooc/iceland_supervooc.c
@@ -1457,6 +1457,9 @@ static int pump_client(const char *parent, struct i2c_adapter **adap, struct i2c
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* iceland: never above stock's highest ask, 7.3 A (the parameter checks enforce it; keep the tables honest too) */
+static_assert(V3B_CAP_MAX <= 73 && V3_STOCK_ASK <= 73 && V4_ENV_A0 <= 73);
+
 static int __init vooc_init(void)
 {
 	const char *bad;
-- 
